## Scope

Red added one test file: `apps/storytime/__tests__/phase4-share-moment.test.tsx`.
Red changed no production source, no week content, and no shipped file.
The shipped week `apps/storytime/content/l2/w01.json` holds `scripts[].share` on all 5 days.
The test reads that file through `weekSchema.parse`.
A case that needs another state makes a deep clone (`structuredClone`).
The approved clone sets `approval.loops` to `{ status: "approved", date: "2026-11-10", words: "test clone" }`.
Each clone passes `weekSchema.safeParse` before it renders.

## Contract for Green

1. `lib/contracts/week.ts` exports `shareSchema` and `shareShotSchema`.
   `scriptSchema` holds `share: shareSchema.optional()`.
   The share object and the shot object are both strict.
   A shot is `{ step: string, media: "photo" | "video" }` and holds no file path.
   A share is `{ shots: 1 or 2 shots, caption: biText }`.
   `caption.en` is not empty.
   `caption.th` may be empty.
2. `lib/share-moment.ts` exports `SHARE_CONSENT_LINE` with `en` and `th` text.
3. `TeacherLessonFlow` shows the moment only when `loopsApproved(week)` is true.
   The gate is the approval only (open question 9).
   A shot shows only at a step of its own day (open question 7).
4. The moment carries `data-share-moment={step.id}`, `data-share-media`, and an element with
   `data-share-label` that differs between photo and video.
   The caption and the consent line show in the active language.

